<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.781 µm on a Holocene Canis lupus (MDCK) apical patch (Canis lupus (Canine, MDCK))",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 1.781 µm on a Holocene Canis lupus (MDCK) apical patch faithfully reproduces Canis lupus (Canine, MDCK) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Canis lupus (Canine, MDCK) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Canis lupus (Canine, MDCK)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Holocene wolf coat spots have wavelength 1.781 µm",
        "does_not_claim: That a second assessor scored this pass",
        "does_not_claim: That each histological polygon is one Turing spot",
        "does_not_claim: That the nanopublications were signed",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivity-ratio sweep and the two negative controls",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Periodic 8-wavelength patch as one apical face",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Time unit of 1 s used only to quote an equivalent diffusivity",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=1.10, gamma=40, D_u=0.8, D_v=9.6 chosen so lambda_c = 1.781e-6 m",
        "reported_in_source: Domestic-dog black coat is a beta-defensin allele, not a measured micrometre wavelength",
        "reported_in_source: MDCK cells are a polarized canine epithelium",
        "reported_in_source: Murray coat pre-patterns are centimetre-scale",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg trimolecular kinetics",
        "reported_in_source: Turing dispersion relation and a finite unstable band of wavenumbers",
        "transfer_boundary: Murray 1981 is not a measurement of Canis lupus at 1.8 µm",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery micrograph has no scale bar; KS = 0.38 compares area shapes, not micrometres" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/canis_lupus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Canis lupus (Canine, MDCK); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing dispersion relation and a finite unstable band of wavenumbers | Schnakenberg trimolecular kinetics | Murray coat pre-patterns are centimetre-scale | MDCK cells are a polarized canine epithelium | Domestic-dog black coat is a beta-defensin allele, not a measured micrometre wavelength; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=1.10, gamma=40, D_u=0.8, D_v=9.6 chosen so lambda_c = 1.781e-6 m | Time unit of 1 s used only to quote an equivalent diffusivity | Periodic 8-wavelength patch as one apical face | Diffusivity-ratio sweep and the two negative controls; transfer_boundary: Murray 1981 is not a measurement of Canis lupus at 1.8 µm | The gallery micrograph has no scale bar; KS = 0.38 compares area shapes, not micrometres; does_not_claim: That Holocene wolf coat spots have wavelength 1.781 µm | That each histological polygon is one Turing spot | That a second assessor scored this pass | That the nanopublications were signed]; phenomenon_size: 1.3 cm (0.01254 m, log10=-1.902 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 1.3 cm to 1.3 cm): 1.3 cm:epithelioid-cyst-buckling" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2006.11.051>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1147880>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-canis-lupus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
